# A searched exact-automorphism class on `Fin 12`: data

The group is `800` permutations of `Fin 12`, the excess permutations that pin it from above are `2`,
and the invariant family it acts on has `27,216` members. How many of those have this group as their
automorphism group *exactly* is not computed and does not need to be: the family is indexed by the
subtype `Magma.tup12R400` of transport tuples passing `Magma.tupOK`, and both sides of the rectangle
are decided by search rather than by enumeration. See `Definability/ExactPrune.lean` for the device
and `Definability/Srch_S12R400.lean` for the data lemmas.

This file is generated by `genrect.py`; it holds only tables, so that `native_decide` -- which
recompiles its whole enclosing module on each invocation -- never has to compile them twice.
-/

